  "name": "Life Skills Profile (LSP-16)",
  "short_name": null,
  "language": "en",
  "description": "The abbreviated Life Skills Profile (LSP-16; Rosen et al., 1989) is a clinician-rated assessment that contains 16 items which provide a key measure of function and disability for people with mental illness. The focus of LSP-16 is on the person’s general functioning, i.e. how the person functions in terms of their social relationships and ability to do day-to-day tasks.",
